assert mm.count(OLDL) == 1; mm2 = mm.replace(OLDL, NEWL)
mw = rd(MW)
DESC_OLD = 'description: "SITTING 19 RUN 1 AT ITS CLEAN POINT 2026-09-27 ('
assert mw.count(DESC_OLD) == 1
mw2 = mw.replace(DESC_OLD, 'description: "SITTING 19 RUN 2 AT ITS CLEAN POINT 2026-09-27 (chapters 29-31 READ lean — every row whole, the ledger %d sources, %d claims, the seat derived, THE CHAIN LAUNCHED; the tail next: the summary, the records, the message; then the commit on his word) — SITTING 19 RUN 1 AT ITS CLEAN POINT 2026-09-27 (' % (NSRC, NCL), 1)
NOTE = ('\n\nSITTING 19 RUN 2 AT ITS CLEAN POINT 2026-09-27 — every row of the three chapters read whole and typed in this run (Onkelos 29, 30, 31 in four files — %d rows %s; the spine 304-305 — %d rows; the nineteen outside rows — %d reread whole, the fresh %s), the import check green in one run (%d bytes, 0 cut misses), the ledger (%d sources, lint 0 after 157:10\'s Hebrew marker was cut and glossed), the manifests (%d claims — I2 at the end analogy\'s three rows, I13 at 334:1, E26 at the two parables, I1 in the ink\'s 31:27; 302:1 seated by 31:10 by a named override), seat_ch29.py derived, the chain scripts derived, THE GATES CHAIN LAUNCHED (the DONE file; the SUMMARY read once at the tail). LESSONS OF RUN 2: (1) THE HEBREW EXPORT\'S VERSE MARKERS MISPRINT TOO — three among the nineteen outside rows (1:1, 302:1, 357:28) mark a verse whose words the row does not quote; the English cites the true verse; a row is seated by ITS OWN QUOTED WORDS, and the union of both files is the instrument that shows the divergence; (2) a Hebrew marker in prose is cut and glossed like any quotation — the lint reads bare Hebrew in parentheses as unglossed; (3) the manifests\' ranges are contiguous — a claim whose design listed a verse apart from its range (31:23 with 31:14-15) folds the verse into its neighbor, and the design\'s distribution of the outside rows yields to the computed seats (six rows moved); (4) the store\'s blank glosses come in two forms — the bare "?" the ink counts and the prefixed "and-?" only the read finds (31:18, 31:23); (5) RUN 1 rowless and RUN 2 all the rows held under the cap — a reading of three chapters with an eight-row spine fits one row run. NEXT: the tail, then the commit on his word (18b + 19).\n'
        % (NO, BYC, NS, NRR, FR, PB, NSRC, NCL))
